  "body": "taking this matrix-dev conversation to github issue: https://matrix.to/#/!XqBunHwQIXUiqCaoxq:matrix.org/$1477765173343911kcHUe:matrix.org\n\nHere is my synapse log while running /sync: [sync-log.txt](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/files/560734/sync-log.txt)\n\nThis began happening after upgrading from 0.16.1-rc1 after realizing that I was pulling the wrong docker file. After that, per discussion in matrix-dev at the time, I was having issues with ujson segfaulting due to issues with Alpine linux. Ported my dockerfile to Fedora Container and started it, and was unable to get /sync to go without using a giant pile of RAM, and even then just barely. This week I ported to postgres after noticing my sqlite3 was 40gib (probably from keeping a few noisy IRC channels bridged, and having my RSS and Twitter bots running 24/7) but decided to port to postgres thinking that would at least help the start up times, and maybe the memory usage. It helped the former, but not the latter, and right now I am using my matrix.org HS account\n",
